1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Two habits to close the tools module: letting the model switch on tools it needs by itself, and reading tool-call cards to understand exactly what happened.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,142
In Settings, General, there's an option to let the model switch on tools it finds itself.

3
00:00:11,142 --> 00:00:17,267
When on, if a task needs a capability, it can enable it mid-conversation instead of you doing it manually.

4
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,000
Handy — but note the boundary.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,878
The important boundary: it can turn on tools that need no credentials — file search, web fetch, and the like — but it cannot connect anything that needs your API key or a sign-in.

6
00:00:24,878 --> 00:00:29,212
So it can help itself to safe capabilities, but it can never quietly wire up something that spends your money or touches an account.

7
00:00:29,212 --> 00:00:30,000
That line is deliberate.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,074
Second habit: read the cards.

9
00:00:31,074 --> 00:00:34,852
When a result surprises you, expand the tool-call card and look at the exact arguments the model used.

10
00:00:34,852 --> 00:00:38,704
Nine times out of ten the surprise is in there — it searched for the wrong term, or read the wrong file.

11
00:00:38,704 --> 00:00:41,000
The answer to “why did it do that” is usually one expand away.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,247
And the theme that runs through everything from here on, worth stating flatly: forty enabled tools choose worse than five.

13
00:00:45,247 --> 00:00:47,092
More options make the model's job harder, not easier.

14
00:00:47,092 --> 00:00:48,171
Keep each chat's toolset tight.

15
00:00:48,171 --> 00:00:52,000
We'll come back to this with agents, workflows, and cost — it's the single most repeated lesson in the course.

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,272
That completes the tools module.

17
00:00:53,272 --> 00:00:57,205
Next we organize work itself — Projects, which stop context from bleeding between unrelated things.

18
00:00:57,205 --> 00:00:58,000
See you in Module 8.

